{
  "name": "Inquiry to CRM",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What this does\n\nSupport email and website form submissions arrive through **different front\ndoors** and are turned into one shape immediately. From there a single matching\nengine decides who each one is from.\n\nSix inquiries in: two matched with confidence, two matched but **not trusted\nenough to file automatically**, two genuinely new.\n\nEvery one of them gets a task, whichever way it went. Nothing is dropped -\nwhich is the actual goal.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "e7000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1980,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## A wrong match is worse than no match\n\nFile Jane's ticket against Daniel's record and you have put one customer's\norder history on another customer's file. Support then answers Jane using\nDaniel's orders.\n\nSo the system has **three** answers, not two:\n\n- **email or order number** matched - file it\n- **phone number only**, or a shared mailbox - a person confirms first\n- **nothing matched** - create a lead marked unverified\n\nThe middle lane is the whole design. Match too strictly and the CRM fills with\nduplicates within a quarter. Match too loosely and you merge two real people.\nLiving between those two failures is the job.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "e7000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1480,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Why four nodes are greyed out\n\nEverything that writes - to the CRM, to the task list, to Slack - is\n**disabled on purpose**. You can run the whole thing against a real inbox,\nread every verdict, and leave nothing behind.\n\nThe two sources and the customer lookup have **pinned data**, so it runs with\nno accounts connected at all.\n\n**Note there is no AI here.** Identity matching is arithmetic, and arithmetic\nshould be deterministic - the same inquiry has to reach the same customer\nevery time. The AI belongs one step later, drafting the reply.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "e7000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -960,
        -420
      ]
    },
